            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0188" n="184" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg184"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.811/1013: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-18T12:00:00-04:00">September 18,
                        1938—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following for Tokyo as No. 326: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Shanghai’s 1225, September 14, 6 p.m., Whangpoo Conservancy. Unless you
                            perceive objection thereto, Department requests that you consult with
                            your British and French colleagues with a view to making separate but
                            similar approaches to the Japanese Foreign Office in such manner as you
                            and your colleagues may deem appropriate. It is suggested that you press
                            for the return of all Conservancy equipment and property to a
                            pre-hostilities status, stressing the damage which the enforced,
                            paralysis of the activities of the Board is causing to the harbor at
                            Shanghai to the detriment of that city and to the shipping and
                            commercial interests there.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeat to Chungking and mail copy to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
